      "abstract": "Abstract:\u201cBolshevism as a Moral Problem\u201d and \u201cTactics and Ethics\u201d were discussions of political ethics closely related to Max Weber\u2019s contemporaneous \u201cPolitics as a Vocation.\u201d They diverged from one another in their historical assessments of possibilities for ethically responsible revolutionary action. They are best understood as developments of an approach to political judgment originally forged by Johann Gottlieb Fichte, whose concerns were associated by Weber with Realpolitik and which continue to animate discussions of \u201cpolitical realism.\u201d Overwriting these concerns as transitional moments in personal conversion narratives or the history of political thought has an inhibiting effect on historical and political judgment.",
